# Normalise line endings. The static build hashes the copied asset bytes to
# derive the service-worker cache name, so a CRLF checkout and an LF checkout
# used to produce two different docs/service-worker.js — which made the "docs/ is
# in sync" CI gate impossible to keep green.
#
# What this actually guarantees: every text file is stored in git as LF (content
# is normalised on the way INTO the index, whatever the worktree holds) and is
# checked out as LF from here on. It does NOT rewrite the worktree you already
# have — a clone made before this file existed still holds CRLF copies until
# those files are next checked out, and git will tell you so ("CRLF will be
# replaced by LF the next time Git touches it"). That is harmless for the CI
# gate, because the gate diffs through the index where everything is LF, and
# because build-static.js normalises line endings again before hashing.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Screenshots and other binaries must never be EOL-converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
